        557.9951171875,
        389.6368713378906
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "fact Langevin step sizes ϵ ∝σ2 are a standard recommen-",
      "bbox": [
        313.1999816894531,
        389.0703125,
        558.0,
        401.59185791015625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "dation in the diffusion literature [5, Algorithm 1]. Here, the",
      "bbox": [
        313.1999816894531,
        404.64129638671875,
        558.0008544921875,
        413.5478515625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "step size choice emerges naturally from the SPC update (5).",
      "bbox": [
        313.1999816894531,
        416.5962829589844,
        558.0010375976562,
        425.5028381347656
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "This connection also sheds light on the benefits of pre-",
      "bbox": [
        323.1629943847656,
        428.5592956542969,
        558.0012817382812,
        437.4658508300781
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "dictive sampling (where we merely choose the best sample)",
      "bbox": [
        313.1999816894531,
        440.5142822265625,
        558.0008544921875,
        449.42083740234375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "[17]. In particular, the unnoised target distribution for pre-",
      "bbox": [
        313.1999816894531,
        452.4692687988281,
        558.0009765625,
        461.3758239746094
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "dictive sampling is a Dirac delta concentrating all probability",
      "bbox": [
        313.1999816894531,
        464.42425537109375,
        558.0009155273438,
        473.330810546875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "mass at global optima [25, Appendix A], leading to a noised",
      "bbox": [
        313.1999816894531,
        476.3802490234375,
        558.0009765625,
        485.28680419921875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "target distribution pσ(U | x) with modes at globally optimal",
      "bbox": [
        313.1999816894531,
        487.617919921875,
        558.01318359375,
        497.936767578125
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "solutions. For this reason, we focus our numerical investi-",
      "bbox": [
        313.199951171875,
        500.29022216796875,
        558.0009765625,
        509.19677734375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "gations primarily on predictive sampling. A more thorough",
      "bbox": [
        313.199951171875,
        512.2452392578125,
        558.0009155273438,
        521.1517944335938
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "exploration of the advantages and disadvantages of other SPC",
      "bbox": [
        313.199951171875,
        524.2001953125,
        558.0009155273438,
        533.1067504882812
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "algorithms is an important topic for future work.",
      "bbox": [
        313.199951171875,
        536.1552124023438,
        513.2188110351562,
        545.061767578125
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "IV. GENERATIVE PREDICTIVE CONTROL",
      "bbox": [
        348.9859619140625,
        554.9031982421875,
        522.2259521484375,
        563.8097534179688
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "The previous section shows that we can think of the mean",
      "bbox": [
        323.1629638671875,
        570.045166015625,
        558.00146484375,
        578.9517211914062
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "of the SPC sampling distribution, ˜Uk, as being drawn from",
      "bbox": [
        313.199951171875,
        579.32177734375,
        557.999755859375,
        591.6017456054688
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "the state-conditioned optimal action distribution",
      "bbox": [
        313.199951171875,
        593.9552001953125,
        508.4866027832031,
        602.8617553710938
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "¯Uk ∼p(U | xk) ∝g (J(U; xk)) .",
      "bbox": [
        368.64593505859375,
        609.9927978515625,
        502.56121826171875,
        622.8526000976562
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "(24)",
      "bbox": [
        541.4053955078125,
        612.6702270507812,
        558.003173828125,
        621.5767822265625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "This leads to a natural question: can we train a generative",
      "bbox": [
        313.199951171875,
        631.38623046875,
        558.0009155273438,
        640.2927856445312
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "model to produce ¯Uk directly? In addition to imitating the",
      "bbox": [
        313.199951171875,
        640.663818359375,
        557.9979858398438,
        653.7417602539062
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "SPC update process, such a generative model",
      "bbox": [
        313.199951171875,
        655.2962036132812,
        499.460693359375,
        664.2027587890625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "pθ(U | xk) ≈p(U | xk),",
      "bbox": [
        385.77294921875,
        673.294921875,
        485.42999267578125,
        683.61376953125
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "(25)",
      "bbox": [
        541.4098510742188,
        674.01220703125,
        558.0076293945312,
        682.9187622070312
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "parameterized by network weights θ, would maintain a",
      "bbox": [
        313.199951171875,
        692.5678100585938,
        558.0008544921875,
        701.6337890625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "structure compatible with the flow matching and diffusion",
      "bbox": [
        313.199951171875,
